Build C++17 <filesystem> into libc++.1.dylib.

The filesystem sources ship in src/filesystem but were left out of the
hand-written cxx_sources list, so the installed libc++ exported zero
std::filesystem symbols. That blocks modern C++ programs from loading under
Darling: the nixpkgs `nix` (2.34.8) dies in dyld with
std::filesystem::directory_iterator::__dereference not found (libnixutil
imports 26 std::filesystem symbols). Add operations.cpp,
directory_iterator.cpp and int128_builtins.cpp, compiled as C++17 (the rest
of libc++ is built as C++11 here).

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 55144f764..9ad27aee7 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -49,6 +49,21 @@ set(cxx_sources
 	src/vector.cpp
 )
 
+# C++17 <filesystem> support. These sources are shipped in src/filesystem but
+# were omitted from the build, so the installed libc++.1.dylib exported zero
+# std::filesystem symbols -- which blocks modern C++ programs (e.g. the nixpkgs
+# `nix`, whose libnixutil imports 26 std::filesystem symbols) from loading.
+# They require C++17, so build just these with -std=c++17 (the rest of libc++
+# is compiled as C++11 here).
+set(cxx_filesystem_sources
+	src/filesystem/operations.cpp
+	src/filesystem/directory_iterator.cpp
+	src/filesystem/int128_builtins.cpp
+)
+set_source_files_properties(${cxx_filesystem_sources}
+	PROPERTIES COMPILE_FLAGS "-std=c++17")
+list(APPEND cxx_sources ${cxx_filesystem_sources})
+
 add_darling_object_library(cxx_obj ${cxx_sources})
 make_fat(cxx_obj)
 
